content.text:
The `/Gallery` subpage works universally — "Yoto Hime" was a redirect to "Youtou Hime" (redirects=1 resolved it). White Daruma has no /Gallery (missing) — N-class darumas have no gallery; skip those.

Rewrite the shikigami listing part of collect-artwork.mjs to query `<en>/Gallery` with redirects=1. Note the redirect resolution: response title may differ (Youtou Hime/Gallery), so map only by response pages — we need to associate back to the shikigami index. Use the `redirects` entries: query redirects list maps from→to. Simpler: match on the no prefix directly! We don't need to know WHICH shikigami the page belongs to — the art file carries the `<no>`: regex `^<no>skin1\.` where no comes from our target list. But batch association still needed for no per page. Use same approach as collect-details: build alias map from j.query.redirects + j.query.normalized.

Rewrite fresh loop:

```js
const galleryTargets = shikiTargets.map((s) => `${s.en}/Gallery`);
for (batch of 25) {
  const j = await fetchRetry(`...prop=images&imlimit=100&redirects=1&titles=...`);
  const byResp = {};
  for (const p of j.query?.pages ?? []) if (p.images) byResp[p.title] = p.images.map(...);
  const alias = {};
  for (const n of [...(j.query?.normalized ?? []), ...(j.query?.redirects ?? [])]) alias[n.from] = n.to;
  for each target: resolve alias, find files matching no+skin1
}
```

For daruma entries: shikigami.json has "en": "White Daruma"? The page "White Daruma" was missing as listed... maybe actual page name differs ("White Darumas1.png" file existed). Whatever — skip missing.

Keep souls logic as-is (65/70 worked). Total re-listing of shikigami galleries = 274 pages / 25 = 11 batches. Reference-redownload: files already downloaded (86) get skipped.

Rewrite collect-artwork.mjs shikigami section.

