Wait — but is M6.png really only 260×291? On the soul page wiki display the soul art looks big. The imageinfo reported size 133KB at 260×291 — that's the "large" version on the wiki, modest resolution.

Hmm — but maybe there's a LARGER original: the 2017 cb URL points to `M6.png` same file. `revision/latest` = current. So 260×291 is all there is.

So the "size wrong" complaint: for Shishio SSR the raw file IS 580×580 like others... So what's "not compact with frame size"?

Let me re-read the user message: "for all Shikigami and soul large photo size are wrong. i will show you for shishio SSR: <wiki link>: large size is <URL 259skin1.png> ... for snow spririt <wiki>: large is <M6.png> but large size photo not compact with frame size please fixed"

I think they demonstrate: these URLs are the correct large images (which we now match) — but the DISPLAY frame is misplaced: image not fitting the frame. Possibly the issue is the modal hero `avatar hero` is 200×200 and:
- 580×580 square arts display OK.
- BUT the M-series soul arts (260×291) display SMALL/blurry? Frame 200×200 for a 260px image = fine.

Hmm wait — maybe the REAL issue: souls on the wiki have a bigger original file — like "Snow Spirit.png" (the icon) vs M6.png (the large). M6 260×291... the wiki soul page displays it at 260px width — matching the natural size. In our modal at 200×200 with object-fit contain → shown 200px wide × 200px tall → the 260×291 fits to 200×224 — slightly cropped scale-down, fine.

Is something actually BROKEN visually? I can't see (window hidden). Let me look at the user's words again: "large size photo not compact with frame size" — maybe the frame is SMALLER than the image (image overflowing?) — avatar.hero 200×200 while modal .md-head... no overflow due to contain.

OR: maybe the user means the CARD view: clicking the card shows... in shikigami cards (grid), clicking test opens modal; the CARD ITSELF (grid card img) is styled by .card img — what size? The card thumbnails use 90px images now still (localImage 90px assets) — those look pixelated? No—cards unchanged.

Honestly the most probable visual complaint: the hero art image WITH TRANSPARENT WHITE SPACE — e.g., many skin1 arts have the character centered in a square canvas with large empty margins at top/bottom, making them look tiny inside a big square frame. E.g., Shishio image fills the canvas vertically — fine. But e.g. some arts are 580×580 with content only in middle 300px → looks small.

Alternatively the REAL issue could be **the .avatar.hero square frame cropping rounded-corner or the frame panel background** (radial gold gradient) mismatching: the border/background styles make the "art" look like it doesn't fit because the image has transparent regions, showing the gradient panel behind — looks off ("not compact with frame").

Best approach: actually LOOK at the modal. The browser window is hidden so screenshot fails... Maybe try again — maybe the desktop window is visible now? Try browser.screenshot once; if blocked, fall back to containment: restyle hero so large art displays at natural-ish size without a rigid square frame: e.g., .avatar.hero { width: auto; height: 260px; } letting aspect flow (260 wide for square arts, ~230 for M6). And soften the frame: keep border.

Let me first ask?? No — the user gave clear instructions "please fixed" for framing. The safest UX: make the hero image keep its natural aspect ratio and be sized to fit the modal nicely: height capped (e.g., 240px), width auto, no square crop constraint, no background panel artifacts. That fixes both square and non-square arts.

Also possibly hoisting the small avatar for character modal conflicts? Character modals use .avatar (132) untouched.

Additionally: since art files are actually WEBP saved with .png extension — browsers don't care (sniffed), all rendered. Fine.

