ESM resolution is relative to the importing file's location, not cwd. Options: install playwright at project root (heavy?), or symlink, or use createRequire? createRequire also resolvable relative to file dir only. Practical: make page-check import via a file URL to the kit's playwright installation:

```js
import { createRequire } from "node:module";
const require2 = createRequire(new URL("../ux-ui-agent-skills/node_modules/", import.meta.url));
const { chromium } = require2("playwright");
```
createRequire takes a base dir: `createRequire(pathToFileURL('../.../node_modules/playwright/'))`? Simpler:

```js
import { createRequire } from "node:module";
import path from "node:path";
const kitReq = createRequire(path.resolve("ux-ui-agent-skills/package.json"));
const { chromium } = kitReq("playwright");
```
createRequire(filename) — filename used as base for resolution. path.resolve("ux-ui-agent-skills/package.json") exists ✓ (package.json is there).

