Now `parts` formatter has month: "short" and year: "numeric" — the year isn't used for ISO anymore but still in parts (unused, harmless — but drop year to keep clean? Keep, harmless — actually remove "year" from parts since unused — it's fine either way; leave it, no lint gate on that).

Now CSS. Insert the clock band styles. Anchor: after `.hero .cta { display: flex; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }` (line 248).

```css
/* ============ live timezone banner (index) ============ */
.clock-band {
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  background: rgb(var(--gold-rgb) / 0.05);
}
.clock-inner { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 1.6rem; }
.clock-zone { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.6rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
.clock-place { color: var(--gold-soft); font-family: var(--font-latin); letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 0.78rem; }
.clock-time { color: var(--cream); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; letter-spacing: 0.06em; font-size: 1.3rem; min-width: 7.2em; text-align: right; }
```
min-width prevents jitter between ticks (tabular-nums already stops digit-width jitter; but when EST shows "EST"→"EDT" widths same. min-width keeps layout stable anyway). Hmm 7.2em of 1.3rem = 9.4rem ~ 150px — fine.

.clock-tz { color: var(--faint); font-size: 0.75rem; letter-spacing: 0.08em; }
.clock-date { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.75rem; letter-spacing: 0.04em; }
.clock-sep { color: var(--vermillion-hi); ... vertical? } "時" glyph as vertical divider: simpler: .clock-sep { color: var(--gold-soft)?? } — vermillion accent nice: color: var(--vermillion-hi); font-size... vertical divider look: make it a hairline: width: 1px; background var(--border); align-self stretch. But I planned glyph 鐘/時. A perpendicular vertical gold hairline with tiny glyph centered may be fussy. Choose: glyph 時 colored var(--vermillion-hi) font-size 0.9rem, wrapped with hairlines via ::before/::after? Overkill. Just glyph; the zones read left/right of it.

Mobile <560px: .clock-inner { flex-direction: column; gap: 0.2rem; } .clock-sep { display: none; } then zones each their own row centered. Also time min-width smaller? At column layout no jitter issue horizontally; keep.

Media query placement: there's an existing @media (max-width or min-width?) ≥720 block (line 825 .hero-inner columns) — the file uses min-width media. For <560 stacking, use a max-width media. Acceptable.

